<title>FINLAND: Rautaruukki wins FIM 55 mln wagon order.</title>
<headline>Rautaruukki wins FIM 55 mln wagon order.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish steel group Rautaruukki Oy said in a statement on Monday it had won orders for railway wagons worth 55 million markka from customers in Sweden and the United Kingdom.</p>
<p>Its Transtech unit would deliver 45 multipurpose wagons to Swedish Norwaggon AB, a private wagon owner, Rautaruukki said, adding the end customer was German Volkswagen-Audi, which would use the wagons to transport car bodies and cars.</p>
<p>Transtech would also also deliver 35 container pocket wagons to British leasing company Tiphook Rail Ltd. The order from Tiphook, which is part of Central Transport Rental Group Plc, included an option for a further 40 wagons, it said.</p>
<p>The deliveries would take place during the first half of 1998, Rautaruukki said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
